# Architecture invariants

Violating any of these is a bug, not a style preference.

## 1. The LLM extracts, the resolver identifies

Intent extraction returns the **spoken string** and a quantity. It never returns a canonical card name, a Scryfall ID, or a set code.

```ts
// BAD - the model invents plausible cards that were never said
{ card: "Lightning Bolt", scryfallId: "e3285e6b-..." }

// GOOD - the model reports what it heard; identity is resolved locally
{ action: "add", spoken: "lightning bolt", quantity: 3 }
```

Card identity is decided **only** by the Resolution context matching against the local Scryfall index. Asking a model to name a card reintroduces hallucination into the one place the system cannot tolerate it.

## 2. Nothing reaches Collection unconfirmed

A resolution below the confidence threshold becomes a pending confirmation on the `VoiceSession`. It does not mutate `Collection`.

## 3. The event log is append-only

`collection_events` rows are never updated or deleted. Corrections are new compensating events. This is what makes undo work.

## 4. No external write outside an explicit sync command

Nothing writes to Archidekt or any other target as a side effect of adding cards. Sync happens only when the user commands it.

## 5. Scryfall ID is the only cross-system key

Every collection entry and every sync row is keyed on `scryfall_id`. Card names are never identity across system boundaries.
